00:05:56.204 --> 00:06:07.039
And then also Nora Ken Tanar asked, can you talk about the challenge of holiday centered episodes and why or how you chose specific holidays to depict like Halloween and Thanksgiving in particular?
然后诺拉·肯·塔纳尔也问，你能谈谈以节日为中心的剧集的挑战，以及你为什么或如何选择特定的节日来描绘，特别是万圣节和感恩节？

00:06:07.039 --> 00:06:16.279
I would say something about that, which is just that you were so excited if you had a great idea for a Halloween episode or a Thanksgiving episode or Christmas episode.
我想说的是，如果你对万圣节剧集、感恩节剧集或圣诞节剧集有好主意，你会感到非常兴奋。

00:06:16.279 --> 00:06:18.115
But if you didn't, it was very daunting.
但如果你不这样做，那就非常令人畏惧了。

00:06:18.115 --> 00:06:21.006
And that's why some years we did them and some years we didn't.
这就是为什么有些年我们这样做了，有些年我们没有这样做。

00:06:21.006 --> 00:06:23.438
It was like, because we did a couple good ones early.
就像，因为我们很早就做了一些好的事情。

00:06:23.438 --> 00:06:27.246
We did a couple really good holiday themed episodes in the first couple of seasons.
我们在前几季中制作了一些非常好的节日主题剧集。

00:06:27.246 --> 00:06:40.048
And when it got a few, a few in and was like, we are not going to live up to our own, not only are we going to not live up to the grand tradition of a Thanksgiving episode, we're not going to live up to the one we did a year ago, then we just wouldn't do it because we're scared.
当有一些人进来的时候，我们就不会辜负我们自己的期望，我们不仅不会辜负感恩节这一集的伟大传统，我们也不会辜负一年前的传统，然后我们就不会这样做，因为我们害怕。

00:06:40.048 --> 00:06:42.297
We're like, we're going to not clear our own bar.
我们就像，我们不会清理我们自己的酒吧。

00:06:42.297 --> 00:06:49.959
So it was was both great if you could kind of use the momentum of a holiday to tell a story, and yet daunting if you didn't have a story that kind of was worthy of it.
因此，如果你能利用假期的动力来讲述一个故事，那就太好了，但如果你没有一个值得的故事，那就令人畏惧了。

00:06:49.959 --> 00:06:55.079
And that's probably, you can go year by year and see the ones where we've clearly followed me to have a good enough idea.
也许，你可以年复一年地去看看那些我们清楚地跟随我的地方，以便有一个足够好的想法。

00:06:55.079 --> 00:07:00.519
