And we obviously know the answer to this, but you can talk a little bit about this.
我们显然知道这个问题的答案，但你可以稍微谈谈这个问题。

00:17:07.327 --> 00:17:11.970
And Subhar, while Harashita asks, is McClaren's bar based on a real bar.
Harashita 问道，Subhar 是根据真实酒吧改编的麦克拉伦酒吧。

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:15.289
McClaren's bar is totally based on a real bar.
麦克拉伦的酒吧完全基于真实的酒吧。

00:17:15.289 --> 00:17:23.170
Down to the design elements, down to the color of the booth, down to the huge murals on the wall, the color of the green lamps on the bar.
细到设计元素，细到展位的颜色，细到墙上的巨幅壁画，细到吧台上绿灯的颜色。

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:36.317
And it was this bar that Carter and I spent a bunch of our early mid-20s going to that was two blocks away from late show with David Lunarman, where we worked and where the entire staff of and crew of that show went out and got super drunk every Thursday night.
我和卡特在 20 岁出头的时候就是在这家酒吧度过的，那里距离 David Lunarman 的深夜秀只有两个街区，我们在那里工作，该节目的全体工作人员和工作人员每周四晚上都会出去喝得烂醉。

00:17:36.317 --> 00:17:38.282
And it was just a huge part of our 20s.
这只是我们20多岁时的很大一部分。

00:17:38.282 --> 00:17:44.427
And so my clearance is a shout out to McGee is still a lab and kicking on 55th Street between Broadway and Ace, I believe.
所以我的许可是对麦基的大声喊叫，麦基仍然是一个实验室，并且在百老汇和艾斯之间的 55 街踢球，我相信。

00:17:44.427 --> 00:17:46.744
And it's kind of the how I met from other bar.
这有点像我在其他酒吧认识的方式。

00:17:46.744 --> 00:17:50.170
They're very much leaned into it being the how I met from other bar.
他们非常喜欢它，就像我在其他酒吧认识的那样。

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:52.588
So if you're ever in New York, you can go there.
所以如果你在纽约，你可以去那里。

00:17:52.588 --> 00:17:54.200
You can probably drink it toots.
你也许可以喝它。

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.870
You're a little I'm not sure exactly if it's a toots.
你有点小，我不确定这是否是嘟嘟声。

00:17:56.870 --> 00:18:00.547
I know they have some drinks called like Robin Sparkles and other things.
我知道他们有一些饮料，比如 Robin Sparkles 之类的。

00:18:00.547 --> 00:18:01.806
The Minnesota title wave.
明尼苏达冠军浪潮。

00:18:01.806 --> 00:18:05.886
And we've been some fan events there and it gets crazy and packed and it's great.
我们在那里举办了一些粉丝活动，活动非常疯狂，人头攒动，非常棒。

00:18:05.886 --> 00:18:07.650
So that up there, if you're in NYC.
如果你在纽约的话，就在那里。

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:30.973
Josh, just maybe a time now, because in the early days of this podcast, many years ago, we talked about the idea of your age now, looking back at the character at that age then and looking back at the portrayal of the character at that age and Craig writing of an older character, looking back at his younger character.
乔什，也许现在只是一次，因为在这个播客的早期，很多年前，我们讨论了你现在年龄的想法，回顾当时那个年龄的角色，回顾那个年龄的角色的刻画，克雷格写了一个年长的角色，回顾了他年轻的角色。

00:18:30.973 --> 00:18:41.210
I just want to pause over this now and just, You have thoughts now about Ted's optimism, whether it's too optimistic, not optimistic enough.
我现在只想暂停一下，只是，你现在对特德的乐观态度有一些想法，无论是太乐观还是不够乐观。

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.410
Do you like where he's going?
你喜欢他要去的地方吗？

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:50.750
How do you feel about Ted as a human, as a 30-year-old human, as now Josh, a 50-year-old human?
作为一个人，作为一个 30 岁的人，以及现在作为一个 50 岁的人，你对 Ted 有何看法？

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:53.059
Yeah.
是的。

00:18:53.059 --> 00:18:55.539
It's a great question.
这是一个很好的问题。

00:18:55.539 --> 00:18:57.839
I look at him that I admire it.
我看着他，我很佩服。

00:18:57.839 --> 00:19:10.109
I think that it's kind of incredible to get to 27 or almost 30 and have that level of faith and naivete on some level.
我认为，能到 27 岁或快 30 岁了，还能在某种程度上保持这样的信念和天真，这有点令人难以置信。

00:19:10.109 --> 00:19:21.730
But I think that Ted and not dissimilar for me, but in totally different ways, like life needed to tenderize him a bit.
但我认为特德对我来说并没有什么不同，只是以完全不同的方式，就像生活需要让他变得温柔一点。

00:19:21.730 --> 00:19:25.170
He needed to get heartbroken a little bit more.
他需要再伤心一点。

00:19:25.170 --> 00:19:29.089
He needed to get scuffed up a little bit more.
他需要再磨损一点。

00:19:29.089 --> 00:19:44.730
I think the best kind of optimism is not like a polyanna-ish denial of darkness or shadow, but one that actually incorporates it and says, life is hard, it'll knock you around.
我认为最好的乐观主义不是波莉安娜式的对黑暗或阴影的否认，而是真正融入它并说，生活是艰难的，它会把你击垮。

00:19:44.730 --> 00:19:57.930
But also, I do have faith and I have faith not just blind faith in some sort of like benevolent you know, a hand that's going to swoop in and fix everything, but I have faith in myself.
而且，我确实有信心，我的信心不仅仅是盲目相信某种仁慈的东西，你知道，一只会猛扑过来并解决一切的手，但我对自己有信心。

00:19:57.930 --> 00:20:00.428
I have faith in myself that I have instincts.
我对自己有信心，我有直觉。

00:20:00.428 --> 00:20:02.650
I've surrounded myself with good people.
我身边都是好人。

00:20:04.329 --> 00:20:08.826
I believe that the universe is a friendly place as Einstein said.
我相信正如爱因斯坦所说，宇宙是一个友好的地方。

00:20:08.826 --> 00:20:11.454
You know, our the only choice we have.
你知道，我们唯一的选择。

00:20:11.454 --> 00:20:14.014
That's the only the biggest question.
这是唯一最大的问题。

00:20:14.014 --> 00:20:17.057
Do we think the universe is friendly or not.
我们认为宇宙是友好的还是不友好的？

00:20:17.057 --> 00:20:23.283
And so I think that it's like adorable, and I don't mean that in like a condescending way.
所以我认为这很可爱，而且我的意思并不是居高临下。

00:20:23.283 --> 00:20:35.665
Like there is something adorable about his naive optimism, but I also can see up ahead, like there's some there's some rapids up ahead for him that he's going to have to navigate.
就好像他天真的乐观态度有些可爱，但我也能预见未来，就像他前面有一些急流，他必须穿越。

00:20:35.665 --> 00:20:45.279
And you know, I imagine it's not unlike being a parent where you look at your kid and you want to create an incredibly safe world for them.
你知道，我想这就像作为父母一样，你看着你的孩子，你想为他们创造一个极其安全的世界。

00:20:45.279 --> 00:20:53.079
And you drop them off at college or they go to their first job and like you're not gonna be able to child-proof the world for them.
当你送他们上大学或者他们去找第一份工作时，你就好像无法为他们保证这个世界的儿童安全。

00:20:53.079 --> 00:20:59.160
Like, you know, did we talk Craig about, I might have told you, Gary Goldman has a great joke.
就像，你知道，我们谈论克雷格时，我可能会告诉你，加里·戈德曼有一个很棒的笑话。

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:08.240
You know, millennials like everyone gets a trophy and people say, well, if everyone gets a trophy, how are they gonna learn how to fail?
你知道，像每个人都获得奖杯的千禧一代，人们会说，好吧，如果每个人都获得奖杯，他们将如何学习如何失败？

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:11.440
And he says, oh, I don't know, Have you ever heard of life?
他说，哦，我不知道，你听说过生命吗？

00:21:11.440 --> 00:21:14.740
You know, just like life will get you.
你知道，就像生活会抓住你一样。

00:21:14.740 --> 00:21:15.740
It'll get you.
它会得到你。

00:21:15.740 --> 00:21:20.480
It'll get you no matter how kind of bubble wrapped you are as a young person.
无论你作为一个年轻人有多么的泡沫包裹，它都会让你受益匪浅。

00:21:20.480 --> 00:21:42.480
So I think that I really, you know, I love Nick Cave so much because he's had so much loss in his life and he's had so much hardship and he's incredibly magnanimous and thoughtful and compassionate and tender, you know, Because I think the hardness of life can either tend to us or harden us.
所以我想我真的，你知道，我非常爱尼克·凯夫，因为他在生活中经历了这么多的损失，他经历了这么多的困难，他非常宽宏、体贴、富有同情心和温柔，你知道，因为我认为生活的艰难要么使我们变得坚强，要么使我们变得坚强。

00:21:42.480 --> 00:21:47.240
And I choose, my hope is that it tenderizes me.
我选择，我希望它能让我变得温柔。

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:55.799
But the temptation to harden up and get tougher and get a little folded armed in cynical is always there.
但变得更强硬、变得更强硬、变得愤世嫉俗的诱惑始终存在。

00:21:55.799 --> 00:21:57.559
The invitation's always there.
邀请函一直都在。

00:21:57.559 --> 00:22:04.700
So for me, Ted is just a reminder like in the last analysis, it's better to err on the side of faith.
所以对我来说，特德只是一个提醒，就像最后的分析一样，最好在信仰方面犯错误。

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:07.089
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:22:07.089 --> 00:22:11.329
Please equip me, all sins are forgiven.
请装备我，所有的罪孽都被宽恕。

